<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clodoald</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 522–c. 560</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Saint Cloud</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clodoald, known as Saint Cloud, was a son of the Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlodomer">Chlodomer of Orléans</a>. When his uncles <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/childebert-i">Childebert I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-i">Chlothar I</a> murdered his brothers in 524 to seize their inheritance, he escaped, later renounced his claim and became a monk. He founded a monastery at Novigentum near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, where he was buried, and the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-cloud">Saint-Cloud</a> is named after him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clodoald.jpg" alt="Clodoald" width="270" height="596" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Daveswagon at en.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saintcloudstatue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
